I finish my cake.
The plate is now empty.
I take the last sip of the tea.
The tea is really very good.
Now I want to go.
I look for the waiter.
He is near another table.
I signal to him.
"Dada, will you come here for a moment?" I ask.
He comes to my table.
"Tell me Madam, do you want anything else?" he asks.
"No, thank you," I say.
"Everything was very tasty."
"I want the bill now."
"Will you please give me the bill?"
"Yes Madam, just a minute," he says.
He goes to the front counter.
He comes back immediately.
"Take this Madam, your bill," he says, handing over a small paper.
I take the bill and thank him.
